# sarvam-mcp

An [MCP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) server for the Sarvam API (lite fixture). It wraps the
[`sarvam`](https://pypi.org/project/sarvam/) Python SDK and exposes one tool per
API method, named `<resource>_<method>`:

- `text_translate`: Translate text between Indian languages and English
- `text_transliterate`: Convert text between scripts without translating it
- `text_identify_language`: Identify the language and script of a piece of text
- `text_to_speech_convert`: Synthesize speech from text
- `speech_to_text_transcribe`: Transcribe an audio file
- `pronunciations_list`: List custom pronunciations
- `pronunciations_create`: Add a custom pronunciation
- `pronunciations_get`: Fetch one custom pronunciation
- `pronunciations_delete`: Delete a custom pronunciation

## Install

```sh
pip install sarvam-mcp
```

Requires Python 3.10 or newer.

## Run

The server speaks MCP over stdio.

```sh
export SARVAM_API_KEY=...
sarvam-mcp
```

Example client configuration:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "sarvam": {
      "command": "sarvam-mcp",
      "env": { "SARVAM_API_KEY": "..." }
    }
  }
}
```

Tool results are JSON. Binary responses are written to the directory in
`SARVAM_MCP_OUTPUT_DIR` (a temporary directory by default) and the tool returns the file's path
and size. Set `SARVAM_BASE_URL` to point the server at a different API host.
